  "additional_concerns": [
    "Candidates node.1bf6918f69c6b37738daeb83, node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e, node.ce439b1cf9ed8301fbb68f94 and node.ea4d19630f8cab09065b1909 convert preserved application processing into a substantive relief exclusion. The circular supports continued processing but does not expressly establish that equivalence. Preserve both interpretations pending the relevant FAQs and existing-process rules.",
    "Candidate node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64 excludes legacy applications from its question's scope. This avoids deciding their relief eligibility; it does not establish that legacy applications are substantively disqualified.",
    "The introduction states immediate effect, while the implementation paragraph specifies 28 November 2025 for measures set out in the FAQs. The specific date supports the proposed commencement assumption, but the supplied source does not resolve every legally relevant assessment or implementation event.",
    "The two missing dependency IDs have no supplied identity mapping. Neither can safely be assigned to the FAQs, forms or existing-process rules.",
    "No candidate establishes notification compliance, filing compliance, post-vetting compliance or an independent approval duty. Home-compliance and product-feature classifications remain supplied judgments rather than implemented legal assessments."
